node_modules/
# Staged sources: someone else's data, up to 1.2GB, re-fetchable by `places stage`.
.stage/
# Working output. The *published* database lives in data/ as gzipped NDJSON and
# is committed on purpose: ODbL's share-alike is discharged by the derived rows
# being available, not by the ETL that would produce them being available.
.build/
.wrangler/
dist/

# Generated from wrangler.jsonc by `bun run types`, which `typecheck` runs first.
# Half a megabyte of runtime declarations that take 0.5s to rebuild — and a
# generated file in git is a generated file that goes stale. This repo has been
# caught by that twice already: a registry item serving an old component, and
# data/ describing a database it was no longer exporting.
worker-configuration.d.ts

# The published database. In R2, not in git — see data/manifest.json.
#
# gzip is already compressed so git cannot delta it: every publish stored a fresh
# 13.4MB forever. `.git` reached 134MB and was mostly twelve copies of
# cities.ndjson.gz, and this repo has already had to filter-repo a 76MB blob once.
#
# ODbL obliges us to make the derived database available. It does not oblige us to
# make it available in git, and a URL discharges it better — the service tests can
# verify the download on every deploy where a commit could only be asserted.
data/*.ndjson.gz
